Q: List of Timezone IDs for use with FindTimeZoneById() in C#? A: <p>Use <a href="https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.timezoneinfo.getsystemtimezones" rel="nofollow noreferrer">TimeZoneInfo.GetSystemTimeZones()</a> method.</p>
<p>Here's a program to retrieve the list of time zone IDs:</p>
<p>The code:</p>
<pre><code>using System;

namespace TimeZoneIds
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            foreach (TimeZoneInfo z in TimeZoneInfo.GetSystemTimeZones())
            {
                Console.WriteLine(z.Id);
            }
        }
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>The results will vary depending on when you run the code, along with the OS version and updates installed.</p>
<p>And a quick and easy PowerShell script:</p>
<pre class="lang-bash prettyprint-override"><code>[TimeZoneInfo]::GetSystemTimeZones() | sort | select Id
</code></pre>
